# Cloud-Based File Storage Frontend Roadmap

## Project Overview
This project is a **cloud-based file storage and sharing system**, similar to Mega or Google Drive.  
- Users can **sign up and log in**.  
- After login, users see a **dashboard** displaying their files and folders.  
- Users can **upload files**, set **permissions**, and share them with others.  
- Account management allows users to **update profile and password**.  
- Permissions include **public links** or sharing with **specific users**.  
- Backend integration (FastAPI) will handle **authentication, file storage, permissions, and encryption** — this roadmap is focused on the **frontend implementation**.  

---

## Frontend Implementation Roadmap

### Context Setup
- [ ] Create `AuthContext.tsx`
  - Stores JWT token and current user
  - Provides `login()`, `logout()`, `getAuthToken()`
  - Wrap `<App />` in `AuthProvider` in `main.tsx`

### Authentication Pages
- [ ] `Login.tsx`
  - Form: email + password
  - Connect to `api/auth.ts` login function
  - Store token + user in `AuthContext`
  - Redirect to Dashboard after login
- [ ] `Register.tsx`
  - Form: email + password
  - Connect to `api/auth.ts` register function
  - Store token + user in `AuthContext`
  - Redirect to Dashboard after registration

### Route Protection
- [ ] `PrivateRoute.tsx`
  - Wrap pages that require login
  - Redirect to `/login` if user not logged in
  - Use `useAuth()` from `AuthContext`

### Dashboard
- [ ] `Dashboard.tsx`
  - Fetch user files/folders using `useFetchFiles` hook
  - Render `FileCard` / `FolderCard` components
  - Handle loading / empty state

### File Upload & Permissions
- [ ] `FileUpload.tsx`
  - File picker or drag & drop
  - Set permissions: public / selected users
  - POST to `/files/upload` endpoint
  - Show success/error feedback
  - Update Dashboard after upload

### Account Settings
- [ ] `AccountSettings.tsx`
  - Allow email/password change
  - Display profile info
  - Connect to `api/users.ts`

### Optional / Bonus Pages
- [ ] `FileDetail.tsx` → single file view + sharing info
- [ ] `Landing.tsx` → welcome page for non-logged-in users
- [ ] `NotFound.tsx` → 404 page

---

## Notes / Best Practices
- Build forms → integrate API → add state/hooks → then style with Tailwind  
- Test each page in isolation before backend is fully ready  
- Use `context` + `PrivateRoute` to secure routes  
- Keep reusable components (`FileCard`, `FolderCard`, `UploadForm`) in `components/`  
- Backend integration (FastAPI) will be implemented **after frontend is functional**
